 "notes": "The dive site on the Schouwen side of the Zeelandbrug, on the north shore of the Oosterschelde: Instap 1 and Instap 2 on the dike, the first three bridge pillars, the rock reef (Breukstenenrif) with the steel slag, sepia sticks, racks and the Ecorif, the 5 and 10 m lines and the three usual routes. The pillars, bridge, dike and the west stairs used for Instap 2 are from OpenStreetMap. The origin is the site's stored point on the water 2.4 km south-west, so the drawing sits north-east of it. Depths of objects follow the depth bands and are approximate; the second pillar is for experienced divers and the whole site is a slack-water dive.",
